    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "\r\nI just remembered having to accomodate this behavior in a previous contribution. I played a bit and indeed the value returned by the input is `undefined` with both empty string and invalid string (ending with separator). I'm fine if we keep it simple (leaving the input empty).\r\n\r\nWhat bothers me more is that the input number type has a locale dependency on what should be a value separator, which we can't control reliably. People should be able to use dot `.` or comma `,`. Maybe we can switch to a text input with pattern validation in the next major or something, even if it's less semantically correct.",
    "commit_id": "10dc88a0281fd30efbcdb04d0babe3cded476d00",
    "created_at": "2023-03-14T10:00:44Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -45,12 +45,14 @@ class RangeInput extends Component<RangeInputProps, Partial<Range>> {\n     });\n   }\n \n-  private onInput = (key: string) => (event: Event) => {\n+  private onInput = (key: keyof typeof this.state) => (event: Event) => {\n     const { value } = event.currentTarget as HTMLInputElement;\n \n-    this.setState({\n-      [key]: Number(value),\n-    });\n+    if (value) {\n+      this.setState({\n+        [key]: Number(value),\n+      });\n+    }",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch/pull/5541#discussion_r1135290563",
